# Dependabot alerts

Triage at https://github.com/thompsonsj/slate-serializers/security/dependabot. Use `gh`, not GitKraken.

1. Trace the parent that pulls the advisory (`npm ls <pkg>`). Prefer a **same-major parent upgrade** or replacing that parent so the patched version arrives normally. Do not add a `package.json` override if a parent bump will do.
2. Skip Nx **major** upgrades unless asked. Same-major Nx patches are fine when they actually clear the advisory.
3. If no compatible parent bump exists and Dependabot opened a security-update PR, **recommend merging that PR** rather than inventing a different pin.
4. Direct `overrides` only when a patched version exists, parents cannot take it, tests still pass, and there is no Dependabot PR. Do not pin to an unpatched latest. Do not `--force` Jest / sprintf-js.
5. If there is no patch, the flagged copy does not contain the vulnerable code, or the package is toolchain-only with no attacker-controlled input, **recommend dismissing** the alert (`tolerable_risk`, `not_used`, or `inaccurate`) instead of a cosmetic lockfile change.
6. Do not mix alert work with release-please PRs. `chore:` / `docs:` do not release; a `fix:` in a linked package does.
